28434"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-174447" :question/id #uuid "2127b35a-3511-5ad2-8ca4-d1c00cbec952" :question/math-academy-id "q-174447" :question/problem "Let $I=Z$ and ${X}_{i}={i-1,\\,i},$ then ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=$" :question/worked-solution "The intersection of a family of indexed sets ${{A}_{i}}_{i\\in I}$ contains all elements that belong to *all* sets in our family:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for all }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=-1,$ we have ${X}_{-1}={-2,-1}$\n\n- if $i=0,$ we have ${X}_{0}={-1,0}$\n\n- if $i=1,$ we have ${X}_{1}={0,1}$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that there is no element that belongs to all the sets. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}=∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-174447/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c1e93acb-6c0b-5263-9df9-9dcc00680845"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-174447"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-184610/selection/40209b98e046e2fc5047800e38733b76cd7a758344696629bf9f7e500ab93d69" :answer/id #uuid "49bafac6-a4e5-54cf-be64-74fcb5e26586" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-184610/selection/40aef41a716249877426126fd877c16e8772d99011fa7c4ead87ff621ecaea8b" :answer/id #uuid "92d5b274-f75b-534e-8792-de21f1347a3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\frac{1}{3},1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-184610/selection/2531b01062963bf17cb1953367062769d91dcfc4519f4f6b120c5de4951d40dd" :answer/id #uuid "b9b7a714-4b46-5fb5-8e07-3ed3063a7ff0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-184610/selection/3f48c5d66954b2c239135dfbfd7897cab553793bde08ceadd4dc08ad57828434" :answer/id #uuid "63c54abd-6de4-58fa