 all elements belonging to *at least one* set in the indexed family:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\in U\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{i}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one }{A}_{i},\\,\\,i\\in I}\n$$\n\nwhere $U$ is a universal set.\n\nThe notation ${⋃}_{i=5}^{\\infty }$ means that our set of indexes is \n${5,6,7…}.$ \n\nLet's now write down a few instances of our indexed sets:\n\n- if $i=5,$ we have ${S}_{5}=[1+\\frac{1}{5},2]=[\\frac{6}{5},2]$\n\n- if $i=6,$ we have ${S}_{6}=[1+\\frac{1}{6},2]=[\\frac{7}{6},2]$\n\n- if $i=7,$ we have ${S}_{7}=[1+\\frac{1}{7},2]=[\\frac{8}{7},2]$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nand so on. \n\nNotice that as $i$ increases, \n\n- the left endpoint of the intervals approaches $1$ but never reaches it, and\n\n- the right endpoint of the intervals equals $2$ for all the sets.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{⋃}_{i=5}^{\\infty }{S}_{i}=(1,2].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-184656/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c1e93acb-6c0b-5263-9df9-9dcc00680845"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-184656"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-184609/selection/04cda31a38923356c3210f1f17a408dbb6b3155f8603d871a7403aecdc4a8f5c" :answer/id #uuid "84ceb6b2-f3f9-5592-847a-a07c621f7bd7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0,2,4,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-184609/selection/2531b01062963bf17cb1953367062769d91dcfc4519f4f6b120c5de4951d40dd" :answer/id #uuid "3b54f3dc-7378-520e-9fc8-2768204bc6fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "∅" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-184609/selection/3f48c5d66954b2c239135dfbfd7897cab553793bde08ceadd4dc08ad57828434" :answer/id #uuid "94945d98-88df-536d-bdaf-f985f1bc5dde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-184609/selection/203f88d94a38bb859e78e84aea518cf34952815758cf391887040455367d62ef" :answer/id #uuid "0d06b4d4-1cdf-564a-9c46-3e0984a